{
  "dom_id": "step-q237553",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/45d4e4ca4f1cdfddcb624dccf32cb053818a2fd70cbb7b5a02d1ff30f9784e2b.png)\n\nIf the model above represents $3$ wholes, use the model to solve the following division problem. Express your answer as a whole number.\n\n$3÷\\frac{3}{7}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into sevenths.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/16e82ebe81e32e4a5d5d273a8dfbdb0669a65b5268ff2653f38ea578d5f52681.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of $\\frac{3}{7}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/b1eb547db76061c7f24a34249554ade3226668e460fac1473e3280fe50807c6b.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/6f79a68dece26e9e430a4b905ee72626fd3ddcbc61dd49b6d8a8d86252dbb31c.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $3$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{3}{7},$ we get $7$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{7}=7.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
